DOCK-003|P0|Core glass material is part of the product identity and architecture choice.|M0 renderer/window decision; backdrop source; M4 material pipeline; rights-safe reference assets.|Given a high-contrast external background, when the Dock is rendered, then captured background detail is demonstrably blurred behind the rounded material and is separately testable from tint, edge, shadow, and icon layers; alpha alone does not pass.|M1 visual criteria; Windows material integration after M0 gate in M4; REF-01 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
DOCK-004|P1|Magnification is a major fidelity feature built on the stable layout/input model.|DOCK-001/002/005; pointer hit testing; M5 animation pipeline.|Given a pointer over or near an icon, when it moves across the Dock, then the intended icon and neighbors change size without losing the correct hit target, overlap, or clipping; curve and timing remain unmeasured.|M1 behavior review; Windows animation/hit-test integration in M5; REF-03 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
