DOCK-024|P1|Folder and Stack representations are useful but must preserve the underlying directory.|DOCK-023; folder item model and view-state persistence in M8.|Given a folder reference, when representation changes between Folder and Stack, then only the Dock presentation changes and all directory contents remain untouched and available.|M1 behavior review; Windows folder/stack integration in M8; REF-02 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
DOCK-025|P1|Stack views provide access to folder contents and need bounded layouts.|DOCK-024; accessible popup surface and monitor work-area model in M8.|Given a stack with more items than fit in the initial view, when expanded as Fan/Grid/List or a supported fallback, then every item remains reachable, selectable, and within the available work area.|M1 behavior review; Windows Stack view integration in M8; REF-02 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
DOCK-026|P1|Predictable folder sorting improves repeated use.|DOCK-024; stable file metadata and sort settings in M8.|Given the same directory snapshot and sort setting, when items are enumerated, then ordering is deterministic with a documented tie-break; inaccessible metadata is handled without dropping the item silently.|M1 behavior review; Windows Shell enumeration integration in M8; REF-02 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
DOCK-027|P0|System item state must be truthful and safe.|Shell Recycle Bin state provider; DOCK-028/029; icon rights/source policy.|Given an empty, non-empty, or unqueryable Recycle Bin, when status is displayed, then the corresponding state is shown or marked unknown; state-query failure never fabricates empty/full.|M1 source review; Windows Recycle Bin integration in M8; REF-02 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
DOCK-028|P0|Opening is basic; emptying is destructive and requires explicit consent.|DOCK-027; Recycle Bin Shell command; confirmation and completion state.|Given a non-empty Recycle Bin, when Open is chosen it opens the system view; when Empty is chosen a clear confirmation appears, cancellation leaves items intact, and successful emptying refreshes the state.|M1 safety review; Windows Recycle Bin integration in M8; REF-02 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
DOCK-029|P0|File deletion/recovery safety is a release-critical data-integrity requirement.|DOCK-027; supported Shell recycle operation; volume/permission/error handling.|Given a supported file dropped onto Trash, when accepted, then it is moved using a recoverable Recycle Bin operation; if unsupported or denied, the source remains intact and no permanent delete fallback is used.|M1 safety review; Windows Shell recycle integration in M8; REF-05 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
DOCK-030|P1|Minimize-to-app behavior relies on window identity and explicit preference.|DOCK-013/014; minimize proxy model in M6/M10; preference persistence.|Given a window owned by a tracked app, when minimized under either configured mode, then its proxy remains uniquely associated and changing the mode does not lose the original window.|M1 behavior review; Windows window/minimize integration in M6/M10; REF-04 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
DOCK-031|P1|A standalone minimized item is an alternate representation, not a separate app.|DOCK-030; file-zone layout DOCK-022; live HWND lifecycle tracking.|Given a window minimized as a separate item, when the item is activated, then that same live window is restored; when the window closes, the item disappears without affecting unrelated windows.|M1 behavior review; Windows window lifecycle integration in M7/M10; REF-04 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
DOCK-032|P2|Custom minimize animation is polish and risks implying control over other apps.|DOCK-030/031; renderer and animation pipeline M5; reduced-motion policy.|Given an eligible minimize/restore action, when an animation is enabled, then Dock-owned visuals complete or safely cancel while the OS window state remains correct; unsupported third-party animation interception is not claimed.|M1 animation review; Windows visual integration in M5; REF-03/04 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
DOCK-033|P0|Auto-hide and reveal affect reachability and desktop obstruction.|DOCK-001/040/041/046; edge hit testing, focus and window policy in M3/M9.|Given auto-hide is enabled, when the pointer reaches the configured edge, then the Dock reveals and later hides according to the documented state model; menus/drag/focus hold visibility and fullscreen suppression never strands recovery.|M1 state review; Windows edge/window integration in M9 after M0 gate; REF-06 Mac sample NOT TESTED.
